---
import EnquiryForm from '../EnquiryForm.astro';
import DublinTourMap from './DublinTourMap.astro';
import DublinReserveForm from './DublinReserveForm.astro';
import WorkshopExploreMore from '../workshops/WorkshopExploreMore.astro';
import { DUBLIN_BOOKING_PAGE_PATH } from '../../lib/booking-urls';
---

<article class="dublin-booking-page marketing-page">
  <header class="dublin-booking-page__header">
    <p class="dublin-booking-page__service-name">
      Private Photo Tour of Dublin City Centre, extra person €50 on the day
    </p>
    <div class="dublin-booking-page__intro">
      <img
        src="/images/osservicesbooking/services/1754270596_1486423754_panoramicireland-1970.jpg"
        alt=""
        width="170"
        height="170"
        loading="eager"
        class="dublin-booking-page__thumb"
      />
      <div>
        <p>
          <strong>Dublin Photo Tours by Panoramic Ireland</strong> — private bespoke photography
          experiences in Ireland's capital since 2006.{' '}
          <strong>Tours are available for any days in 2026, 2027 and beyond — subject to availability.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Join Irish professional travel photographer Darren for a private guided photo tour of Dublin,
          one of Europe's most rewarding capital cities — compact, flat, and full of hidden angles along
          the River Liffey and beyond. Darren has been commissioned by <strong>The New York Times</strong>,{' '}
          <strong>Ritz-Carlton</strong>, <strong>easyJet</strong>'s Traveller Magazine and{' '}
          <strong>Eater</strong>. His images have also appeared in The Sunday Times and The Irish Times.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every tour is private — just you and your group — and entirely flexible. There are many routes
          through Dublin depending on what you prefer, and Darren will tailor the experience on the day.
          Please note this tour covers Dublin City, not its coastline.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <figure class="pi-figure">
    <img
      src="/images/gallery-dublin-photography-workshop/dublin-hapenny-bridge-liffey-night-photography-tour-panoramic-ireland-3506.jpg"
      alt="Ha'penny Bridge illuminated at night over the River Liffey, Dublin — long exposure photography by Panoramic Ireland"
      width="1200"
      height="800"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </figure>

  <section class="dublin-booking-page__section">
    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <p>
      Dublin rewards the patient photographer at every turn. The <strong>Ha'penny Bridge</strong> — Dublin's
      most iconic crossing — comes alive at blue hour when the cast-iron railings glow against the Liffey and
      the city lights mirror in the water below. <strong>Trinity College</strong> offers centuries of
      architectural history in a single courtyard, from the Parliament Square façade to the hidden corners most
      visitors never find. The <strong>Georgian streets</strong> around Merrion Square and the Grand Canal
      give you some of the finest 18th-century architecture in Europe — Dublin's colourful doors, fanlight
      windows, and lamp-lit pavements that reward a slower pace. <strong>Temple Bar</strong> and the cobbled
      streets of the cultural quarter offer colour, energy and photographic character at any hour. The{' '}
      <strong>Custom House</strong> on the north quays is one of James Gandon's finest neoclassical buildings,
      and its reflection in the Liffey on a still morning is extraordinary. And the quays along the{' '}
      <strong>River Liffey</strong> — from the Famine Memorial to the Samuel Beckett Bridge — give you the full
      sweep of Dublin's relationship with its river. At the heart of it all, Dublin Castle is a fine place to
      stop in the middle of the city for a few moments to look for architectural details.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a guide to the possibilities, not a fixed itinerary. Every tour is shaped on the day around what
      you want to shoot, how much time you have, and where the light is best. Tour stops are exterior/public-space
      photography locations; admission tickets are not included but we don't usually venture into ticketed places.
    </p>
    <p>
      This tour is priced for two people. For €50 extra you can bring a friend, or make it a dedicated one-to-one
      photography experience. Children under 16 go free.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prefer a firm hold on a date? Use <a href="#reserve">Reserve this Experience</a> below. Or enquire with
      preferred dates and any questions — Darren will reply by email with availability and next steps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="dublin-booking-page__section">
    <h2>Every tour is unique — the route map below is a guide only.</h2>
    <p>We can cover whatever you like in Dublin, at any time of day.</p>
    <p>
      In summer, a late-afternoon start becomes our <strong>Evening &amp; Night Photography Experience</strong> —
      available May to August when Dublin stays bright until 10:30pm. Begin in golden hour light, shoot through
      blue hour, and finish with Dublin's spectacular urban nightscape — illuminated bridges, Liffey
      reflections, Temple Bar after dark. A completely different city, and worth every minute.
    </p>
  </section>

  <figure class="pi-figure">
    <img
      src="/images/gallery-darren-photographer-about/samuel-beckett-bridge-convention-centre-liffey-reflection-9089-Edit-panoramic-ireland.jpg"
      alt="Samuel Beckett Bridge and Convention Centre reflected in the River Liffey at dusk, Dublin — photography by Panoramic Ireland"
      width="1200"
      height="800"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </figure>

  <section class="dublin-booking-page__reviews">
    <p>Read what T.N. from Australia had to say recently in this verified review:</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        <em>
          "Darren is a terrific guide and a very kind and personable host. He took me on a great walking tour
          of Dublin City where we explored and took some great photos of several sights off the tourist trail.
          Darren is genuinely passionate about Dublin city as he is about his craft and he was very generous
          with sharing his abundant knowledge and experiences. I had a really enjoyable day and took many tips
          away with me that I will apply in my photography going forward. I highly recommend this experience to
          anyone at all, local or from abroad, who is interested in photography and is after a unique
          personalized experience photographing Dublin city."
        </em>
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>And D.A. from USA:</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        <em>
          "Darren is a fantastic professional photographer and a great, kind and friendly host. Darren took me
          on a really fun tour of Dublin and shared his photography techniques, thoughts and ideas with me.
          Darren is extremely knowledgeable about photography, art, architecture and history and is a very
          patient guide. Highly recommend this experience, it's definitely one of the best out there!"
        </em>
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <DublinTourMap />

  <ul class="dublin-booking-page__meta" aria-label="Tour price and duration">
    <li><strong>€500.00 EUR</strong></li>
    <li><strong>4h 30m</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Guide: Darren McLoughlin</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <DublinReserveForm
    tourId="dublin-photo-tour"
    priceLabel="€500"
    groupLabel="For 2 people"
    durationLabel="4h 30m"
    extraGuestLabel="+€50 per extra guest"
  />

  <section class="dublin-booking-page__enquiry" aria-labelledby="enquiry-heading">
    <h2 id="enquiry-heading">Or enquire without picking a time</h2>
    <p class="dublin-booking-page__enquiry-note">
      Send preferred dates, group size, and what you'd like to photograph if you’d rather not reserve a
      slot yet.
    </p>
    <EnquiryForm sourcePage={DUBLIN_BOOKING_PAGE_PATH} confirmationId="dublin-enquiry-sent" />
  </section>

  <WorkshopExploreMore />
</article>

<style>
  .dublin-booking-page {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__service-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    color: var(--color-forest-900);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-l);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__thumb {
    max-width: 170px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__section h2,
  .dublin-booking-page__section h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__reviews blockquote {
    margin: var(--space-s) 0 var(--space-m);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-gold-500);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-l) 0;
    padding: var(--space-s) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    font-size: var(--step-small);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__enquiry {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__enquiry h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .dublin-booking-page__enquiry-note {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .dublin-booking-page__intro {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
